.\" kari.1 — manual page for kari
.\" Man page for kari: terminal media player frontend.
.\"
.\" Conventions:
.\"   .B  bold (commands, options, key names)
.\"   .I  italic (arguments, placeholders)
.\"   .BR mixed bold/roman (option + argument on same line)
.\"   .PP new paragraph
.\"   .TP tagged paragraph (option lists)
.\"   .RS/.RE relative indent for sub-lists
.\"
.TH KARI 1 "October 2026" "kari" "User Commands"
.\" ────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH NAME
kari \- terminal frontend for streaming anime, movies, and TV shows
.\" ────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kari
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ QUERY ]
.\" ────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kari
(狩り, \fIhunt\fR) is an interactive terminal user interface that searches
multiple streaming sources in parallel and plays media through an external
player (MPV, IINA, or VLC).
.PP
Invoking
.B kari
without arguments opens the interactive TUI.
Passing a
.I QUERY
string pre-fills the search input and executes the search immediately, e.g.
.RS
.B kari "frieren"
.RE
.PP
Kari tracks watch history and resume positions automatically via MPV's local
IPC socket.
It scrobbles to AniList (anime) and Trakt.tv (movies, TV) when authorized,
selects subtitles from provider-embedded tracks and falls back to
OpenSubtitles, and injects skip chapters (opening, ending, recap, preview)
into MPV for supported titles.
.\" ────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version string and commit hash, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-U ", " \-\-update
Fetch the latest release from GitHub and replace the running binary
in-place, then exit.
Requires write permission to the directory containing the
.B kari
binary.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short usage summary and exit.
.\" ────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH INTERACTIVE KEYS
All keybindings are active inside the TUI.
Keys are context-sensitive; some bindings are only available on specific
screens (e.g. episode list, history, settings).
.SS Navigation
.TP
.BR "↑ / ↓" " or " "j / k"
Move selection up or down.
.TP
.B Enter
Confirm selection: open series → select episode → launch player.
.TP
.BR Esc " / " Backspace
Go back to the previous screen.
.TP
.B Space
Execute a search for the current input text.
.TP
.BR Tab " / " Shift+Tab
Cycle the active content category forward or backward:
.B Anime → Movies → TV → Cartoons → Jellyfin\c
\&.
.TP
.B /
Enter filter mode to narrow the current list.
.TP
.B Ctrl+H
Return to the home / search screen from any depth.
.TP
.BR g " / " G
Jump to the first / last item in the current list.
.TP
.B ?
Toggle the in-TUI keybinding help overlay.
.SS Playback
.TP
.B n
Play the next episode in the series.
.TP
.B A
Toggle auto-play (automatically advance to the next episode on completion).
.TP
.B a
Toggle Sub / Dub audio mode (Anime mode only).
.TP
.B r
Restart the current episode from the beginning, discarding the saved
resume position.
.TP
.B Ctrl+P
Switch the active media player (cycles through detected players).
.SS Downloads
.TP
.B d
Download the selected episode via
.BR yt-dlp (1),
with optional
.BR aria2c (1)
acceleration.
.TP
.B x
Stop or cancel the active download.
.TP
.B Space
Toggle selection of an episode for batch download (download list screen).
.TP
.B Ctrl+A
Select all episodes for batch download.
.TP
.B Ctrl+D
Deselect all episodes.
.TP
.B D
Batch-download all selected episodes.
.SS History & Settings
.TP
.BR h " / " H
Open the watch history screen.
.TP
.B m
Mark the current entry as fully watched.
.TP
.BR s " / " S
Open the settings screen (Trakt, AniList, subtitles, theme, language
filters, skip behavior).
.TP
.B t
Show the anime status overlay (airing status, episode count).
.SS Application
.TP
.B Ctrl+D
Toggle the real-time debug log panel.
.TP
.BR q " / " Ctrl+C
Quit kari.
.\" ────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH CONTENT CATEGORIES
Pressing
.B Tab
cycles through five categories.
.TP
.B Anime
Searched via Anikoto (primary) and AniVault (secondary, AniList-indexed).
Supports Sub/Dub audio selection and AniList scrobbling.
.TP
.B Movies
Searched via Movy.sx (primary) and Pengu (secondary, TMDB-indexed).
Supports Trakt scrobbling.
.TP
.B TV
Same providers as Movies.
Supports Trakt scrobbling.
.TP
.B Cartoons
Same providers as Movies.
.TP
.B Jellyfin
Your personal Jellyfin server.
Requires
.B JELLYFIN_URL
and
.B JELLYFIN_API_KEY
to be set.
.\" ────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B KARI_PLAYER
Force a specific player.
Accepted values:
.BR mpv ", " iina ", " vlc .
Default: auto-detected from
.BR PATH .
.TP
.B KARI_DOWNLOAD_DIR
Directory where downloaded episodes are saved.
Default:
.I ./downloads
(relative to the working directory at launch).
.TP
.B KARI_LOG_FILE
Path for the application log file.
Default:
.IR ~/.config/kari/kari.log .
The log rotates automatically at 10\ MB.
.TP
.B KARI_LOG_DEBUG
Enable verbose debug logging.
Set to
.B true
or
.BR 1 .
Default:
.BR false .
.TP
.B KARI_LOG_STDERR
Mirror logs to standard error in addition to the log file.
When standard error is connected to an interactive terminal, output is
automatically suppressed to prevent corrupting the TUI.
Redirect standard error
(e.g.\&
.BR "kari 2> kari.err" )
or stream from another terminal to capture logs.
Set to
.B true
or
.BR 1 .
Default:
.BR false .
.TP
.B JELLYFIN_URL
Your Jellyfin server base URL, e.g.\&
.IR https://jellyfin.example.com .
Setting this activates the Jellyfin category.
.TP
.B JELLYFIN_API_KEY
Jellyfin API key generated from the Jellyfin dashboard
(Dashboard → API Keys).
.TP
.B TMDB_API_KEY
Custom TMDB v3 API key.
Kari uses a built-in rotating key pool when this is unset.
.TP
.B OPENSUBTITLES_API_KEY
OpenSubtitles REST API key for fallback subtitle lookup.
.TP
.B OPENSUBTITLES_USERNAME
OpenSubtitles account username.
Required when
.B OPENSUBTITLES_API_KEY
is set.
.TP
.B OPENSUBTITLES_PASSWORD
OpenSubtitles account password.
Required when
.B OPENSUBTITLES_API_KEY
is set.
.TP
.B KARI_DISCORD_APP_ID
Override the Discord Rich Presence application ID.
Intended for forks and development builds.
.\" ────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/kari/kari.log
Default application log file (rotates at 10\ MB).
.TP
.I ~/.config/kari/settings.json
Persisted user settings: active media category, theme, accent color,
subtitle language preference, enabled providers, scrobble tokens, skip
behavior.
.TP
.I ~/.config/kari/history.json
Watch history database (series, episode, timestamp, resume position,
audio mode).
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/man/man1/kari.1
Default man page installation path (macOS / Linux).
.\" ────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH MEDIA PLAYERS
kari communicates with the media player via a local Unix IPC socket
(MPV / IINA) to track the playback position for accurate resume support.
VLC is supported for playback but does not report position back.
.TP
.B mpv
Recommended.
Full IPC position tracking, smart skip chapters injected as seekbar
chapters, custom HTTP headers (Referer, Origin, cookies), and subtitle
track injection.
Supported on Linux, macOS, Windows, and Android (Termux + MPV Android).
.TP
.B iina
macOS only.
MPV-based; position tracking supported via the same IPC protocol.
.TP
.B vlc
Linux, macOS, Windows.
Playback supported; no IPC position tracking (resume is approximate).
.TP
.B MX Player
Android only.
Launched via Android intents through Termux.
.\" ────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH SKIP ENGINE
kari's hybrid skip engine queries four sources in parallel for each episode:
.PP
.RS
.PD 0
.IP \(bu 2
.B SkipDB
.IP \(bu 2
.B IntroDB
.IP \(bu 2
.B Anime-Skip
(GraphQL)
.IP \(bu 2
.B AniSkip
.PD
.RE
.PP
When skip data is found, virtual chapters (Opening, Ending, Recap, Preview)
are injected into MPV's seekbar, and a context-aware OSD prompt
(\fIPress Enter to Skip\fR) appears at the appropriate playback position.
Skip behavior can be toggled in the settings screen (\fBs\fR).
.\" ────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH DOWNLOADS
The
.B d
key downloads the selected episode using
.BR yt-dlp (1).
When
.BR aria2c (1)
is available on
.BR PATH ,
kari automatically enables 16-connection acceleration for significantly
faster downloads.
Files are saved to
.B KARI_DOWNLOAD_DIR
(default
.IR ./downloads ).
.\" ────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH SCROBBLING
Kari supports native device-flow OAuth authorization for two services.
No API tokens need to be copied manually; the TUI guides you through the
device-flow URL and code.
.TP
.B AniList
Tracks anime watch progress.
Authorize from the Settings screen (\fBs\fR → AniList).
.TP
.B Trakt.tv
Tracks movie and TV watch history.
Authorize from the Settings screen (\fBs\fR → Trakt).
.\" ────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Open kari interactively:
.B kari
.TP
Search for "Attack on Titan" immediately on launch:
.B kari "Attack on Titan"
.TP
Print the installed version:
.B kari --version
.TP
Self-update to the latest release:
.B kari --update
.TP
Enable verbose debug logging for a session:
.RS
.B KARI_LOG_DEBUG=true kari
.RE
.TP
Force MPV as the media player:
.RS
.B KARI_PLAYER=mpv kari
.RE
.TP
Use a custom download directory:
.RS
.B KARI_DOWNLOAD_DIR=~/Videos kari
.RE
.\" ────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Logs are written to
.I ~/.config/kari/kari.log
and rotate automatically at 10\ MB.
.PP
The suggested way to stream logs in real time without corrupting the TUI
is redirecting standard error to a separate terminal using its TTY device
(run
.B tty
in Terminal 1 to obtain its path, e.g.\&
.IR /dev/pts/2 ):
.RS
.B KARI_LOG_STDERR=true kari 2> /dev/pts/2
.RE
.PP
Alternatively, stream the log file from another terminal:
.RS
.B tail -f ~/.config/kari/kari.log
.RE
.PP
To capture logs to a file:
.RS
.B KARI_LOG_STDERR=true kari 2> kari.err
.RE
To enable verbose debug logging:
.RS
.B KARI_LOG_DEBUG=true kari
.RE
.\" ────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal exit.
.TP
.B 1
Startup failure (logging init failed, fatal configuration error) or the
application exited with an internal error.
